ok: a test declaring the dep
ok: a test omitting the dep
ok: a test with deps but not this one
ok: the dep is found wherever in deps it sits
ok: a multi-test stanza is one site naming both
ok: inline tests declare the dep inside their own field
ok: an inline-test field with no deps at all
ok: a library's own deps are not the inline tests' deps
ok: a plain library is not a site
ok: an executable is not a site
ok: a rule running an executable is a site
ok: a rule running an executable through a named dep is one too
ok: a nested action does not hide the executable
ok: a rule running no executable is not a site
ok: a rule running a non-OCaml tool is not a site
ok: an alias stanza is read like a rule
ok: a stanza inside a comment is not a stanza
ok: a config named in a comment does not declare it
ok: a config named in a string is not a dep
ok: an executable named in a comment does not make a rule a site
ok: a subdir's stanzas are the same kinds of site
ok: a nested subdir names the path it applies to
ok: stanzas outside the subdir keep the dune file's own directory
ok: stanzas are reported in file order
ok: copies the config -- a copy_files stanza
ok: copies the config -- the short spelling
ok: copies the config -- a copy_files inside a subdir names that directory
ok: copies the config -- copying something else
ok: copies the config -- no copy_files at all
ok: unclassified heads -- a classified stanza
ok: unclassified heads -- a stanza that runs nothing
ok: unclassified heads -- a cram stanza
ok: unclassified heads -- an include, whose contents the scan never sees
ok: unclassified heads -- inside a subdir, too
ok: unclassified heads -- something that is not a stanza at all
ok: refused -- a block comment
ok: refused -- a datum comment
